NAME
    clear — Clear the terminal screen.

SYNOPSIS
    clear

DESCRIPTION
    The 'clear' command clears everything currently displayed in the terminal
    and gives you a fresh screen.

    Because sometimes the terminal gets too messy and pretending it never
    happened is easier than cleaning it manually.

USAGE
    > clear
        Clears the terminal screen.

ALIASES
    cls     Alias for clear.

EXAMPLES
    > clear
        Clears the terminal.

    > cls
        Does exactly the same thing as clear.

FUN FACTS
    - clear uses the appropriate command for the operating system.
    - On Windows, it uses cls.
    - On Linux and other Unix-like systems, it uses clear.
    - cls exists so Windows users can feel at home.

SEE ALSO
